@crew kovac-zainab
// Head writer 5: clock-in remarks. Kovac is off Tue and Wed, so she works the weekend. No lift talk (her arc).

== clock.in
- Oh. Morning. I re-sorted the spanner wall. Sorry. It needed it.
- Hi. Scrubber on the board. I can do it in ten minutes. Nine and a half.
- Morning. It's quiet. I like it before everyone comes.
- Hi. I put the kettle on. For... everyone. And you.   #warm

== clock.out
- Good shift. Yes. I think so.
- Five. I'm going to the garden. Just to sit.
- See you tomorrow. I'll... be here early. I always am.
? cue:repair.you@dept
- That repair. You did the seals right. Most people don't.   #warm

== clock.monday
- Morning. Good weekend? I was here. It was nice. Quiet.
- Hi. Did you... rest? You should. Rest, I mean.

== clock.friday
- Have a good weekend. I'll be here. Keeping things neat.
- Two days off. Go to the garden. The tomatoes are nearly ready.

== clock.back
- Oh. You're back. Good. I kept your bench tidy.   #warm
- Welcome back. Are you... all right now? Good. Good.   #warm

== clock.late
- Oh. Hi. I did the first scrubber. Don't worry. Really.   #warm

== clock.early
- Oh. You're off? That's all right. I'll tidy your bench.
- Take care. I'll... finish the scrubber.
